From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spottedleaf <Spottedleaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 02:56:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Delay close callbacks for chests

The logic for chests may invoke block updates, which may not
be safe to perform. For example, inventory closing due to
player logout (which restricts chunk loading due to being
inside an entity status callback) or during shutdown (which has
chunk loading restrictions due to the chunk system being halted).

Container state changes are observable from the advancement callback that
follows a block use, so opening must remain synchronous for datapack GUIs.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BarrelBlockEntity.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BarrelBlockEntity.java
index a47b79c188f459e8b8f8cf0872a610b461ebde59..5ddfc7c9df08e9abedcb0fbaa0f614a804ee4059 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BarrelBlockEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BarrelBlockEntity.java
@@ -60,6 +60,13 @@ public class BarrelBlockEntity extends RandomizableContainerBlockEntity {
     private static final Component DEFAULT_NAME = Component.translatable("container.barrel");
     private NonNullList<ItemStack> items = NonNullList.withSize(27, ItemStack.EMPTY);
     public final ContainerOpenersCounter openersCounter = new ContainerOpenersCounter() {
+        // Paper start - delay close callbacks
+        @Override
+        public boolean delayCallbacks() {
+            return true;
+        }
+        // Paper end - delay close callbacks
+
         @Override
         protected void onOpen(final Level level, final BlockPos pos, final BlockState state) {
             BarrelBlockEntity.this.playSound(state, SoundEvents.BARREL_OPEN);
